<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wahriz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wahriz was a Sasanian Persian commander sent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khosrow-i">Khosrow I</a> around 570 to help the Himyarite noble <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sayf-ibn-dhi-yazan">Sayf ibn Dhi Yazan</a> drive the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aksumite-empire">Aksumites</a> out of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>. Leading a small force, he defeated the Aksumite army and killed its ruler, Masruq, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abraha">Abraha</a>. Yemen became a Sasanian dependency, and Wahriz later governed it himself.</p></div>
